{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/98434-demons-and-meditation","id":98434,"title":"Demons and Meditation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T10:08:13-07:00","id":98434,"title":"Demons and Meditation","content":"I was wondering how to make Meditative Mind matter for Demons as one of my players dumped 4 merit points into it. But meditation doesn't seem obviously relevant to Demons as it's primarily used for breaking points. I thought of doing a direct port and applying the bonus to Compromise Rolls but it just doesn't seem to fit mechanically. Even if the compromise roll is due to the cover's equivalent breaking point it still doesn't make sense that meditation for a couple of hours would make it harder for the God-Machine to find you.<br /> <br /> Clearly there is some use that demons get from Meditative Mind as Comrade West has it. So my current thinking is to use meditation to give a bonus on the <u>Intelligence+Wits</u> roll to guess the next Cipher Key. I am justifying this based on this paragraph on p.33, which seems to match the description of searching for the Cipher (even though it's in a different section):<br /> <br /> &quot;While many demons despair of ever understanding their own origins, some view the search as their primary purpose. These demons <b>meditate</b>, experiment upon themselves, and vivisect captured angels, all in the hope of learning more about what they really are.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Or is this unnecessary and Meditation has some more direct use that I am ignoring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":""